## CRITICAL: Fix Root Cause — Never Shortcut Quality Gates

When quality gates fail, FIX THE ROOT CAUSE.

**Only Audited Exceptions May Pass:** basedpyright must pass. Only bypasses explicitly documented in each repo's `QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md` (sections 2.1, 2.2, 2.3) are allowed. Never relax rules, add baseline files, or downgrade reportAny/reportUnknown*.

**CRITICAL - Basedpyright Execution Rules:**
- ❌ NEVER run `basedpyright .` from workspace root - it will hang indefinitely
- ❌ NEVER run basedpyright on multiple repos in parallel - causes hangs
- ✅ ALWAYS run per-repo with timeout: `cd <repo> && timeout 60 basedpyright <source_dir>/`
- ✅ ALWAYS process repos sequentially (one at a time)
- If timeout fires (>60s), kill process and report which repo failed
- Run on source directory only, not tests/ (e.g., `basedpyright instruments_service/`)

NEVER:
- Skip tests to pass gates
- Add `|| true` to bypass failures
- Comment out failing tests
- Remove parallel execution instead of adding pytest-xdist

Codex: `06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md`

**UI repos:** TypeScript UIs run `tsc --noEmit` + ESLint, NOT pyright/ruff/pytest. Codex: `06-coding-standards/quality-gates-ui-typescript.md`, `.cursor/rules/ui-quality-gates-typescript.mdc`

**Quality Gate Performance:** Quality gates must complete in <3 minutes locally. Use pytest-xdist for parallel execution, synthetic fixtures, and skip slow tests in quick mode.

